# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Hey Otis — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is BUNDLED INTO THE CLIENT JS and readable
# by anyone who inspects the app. Only put values here that are safe to
# expose publicly. See store-assets/security/SECRETS.md for the full
# taxonomy of what lives where.

# Supabase project URL — public by design.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Supabase *anon* key — public by design. Role=anon + RLS policies enforce
# access. NEVER put the service_role key here.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# NOTE — do NOT add an Anthropic API key here.
# Anthropic calls go through the `claude-proxy` Supabase Edge Function,
# which reads the key from its own Deno.env (server-side secret). If you
# see a stale `EXPO_PUBLIC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in an older .env file,
# delete it — it is no longer used and must not be set client-side.

# PostHog project API key (starts with phc_…). Public by design —
# PostHog client keys are write-only and event ingestion is rate-limited
# per project. Leave blank to disable analytics entirely (events become
# no-ops). Tracking stays opted-out until the user accepts the
# consent gate in onboarding.
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Host: https://us.i.posthog.com (default) or https://eu.i.posthog.com.
EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
